Original commit body from 35a02c33ad411e3d3cc68ab022e16b0dae93e568:

find_objc_files took every *.h in a repository and C or C++ took them
too, so each header was parsed by two grammars whatever its dialect.
Each grammar's failures on the other dialect surfaced as partial-parse
rows (WI-bulaz), and the C grammar read ObjC headers into wrong symbols
and edges (@property and API_AVAILABLE(ios(...)) as calls, an NS_ENUM
member as a typedef). The C and C++ rules (WI-rizas) also disagreed on
what makes a repo C++, so a repo with .hpp and no C++ source left its
.h files to neither.

header_owner.py is the one rule all three finders apply: a header with
ObjC-only syntax at a line start (@interface/@protocol/@class/@property/
@end/@implementation/@import, #import) is ObjC's; any other is C++'s when
the repo holds any C++ file, else C's. C now registers its finder, so
profile's per-language file counts match what each analyzer parses.

Measured, pinned worktree A (433c90f9f1) vs B, 8 repos:
- partial-parse rows removed: sherpa-onnx 426, SDWebImage 156,
  whisper.cpp 106, CocoaLumberjack 91, AFNetworking 29, fmdb 11, crun 8,
  linuxkit 1
- calls removed, every one read from a wrong-dialect .h (none from a
  .c/.cpp/.m): SDWebImage 165, CocoaLumberjack 56, whisper.cpp 23,
  fmdb 10, AFNetworking 7; crun, linuxkit, sherpa-onnx unchanged
- the classifier, checked on 27 local repos: every ObjC-repo header it
  misses is macros or C-syntax declarations; every C-repo header it hits
  is a real ObjC or mixed header

A first cut also gave UNMARKED headers of a pure-ObjC project to ObjC.
Measurement refuted it: the ObjC analyzer emits no C constructs, so
fmdb's fts3_tokenizer.h lost its sqlite3_tokenizer_module struct.
Unmarked headers are C syntax by definition and now go to C/C++.

Costs, stated: C declarations inside ObjC headers are no longer
extracted (nothing outside a header referenced any, in the repos
measured); the ObjC analyzer records only #import, so #include in ObjC
headers yields no import edge (whisper.cpp -4); a header whose only ObjC
is past its first 64 KB stays C++ (whisper.cpp miniaudio.h: -7 ObjC
methods).

Relocates two module_key_axis line pins moved by the edits.

Addresses WI-somod.

